	"history": "At Giza we gazed up at the Great Pyramid of Khufu. It once stood about 146 metres tall, and for nearly four thousand years nothing built by human hands stood taller; that is, until the spire of Lincoln Cathedral rose in England, around 1311. Roughly 2.3 million blocks of stone went into it, a number we must admit we did not try to verify.",
